window.META_MATH = {"subject": "Modern Algebra", "projects": [{"id": "MA-01", "slug": "lagranges-theorem", "title": "Lagrange’s Theorem", "target": "<p>For a finite group\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>\nand subgroup\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H\\le G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|=[G:H]|H|</annotation></semantics></math>,\nhence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|H|</annotation></semantics></math>\ndivides\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>G is finite and H is a subgroup. Left cosets are sets\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gH=\\{gh:h\\in H\\}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthey are not being endowed with a quotient group structure. Use group\ninverses, bijections, equivalence classes, and finite counting.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Cosets partition the group", "proof": "1. Every g belongs togH since1∈H.\n\n2. If gH∩kH containsx=gh₁=kh₂, then k⁻¹g=h₂h₁⁻¹∈H.\n\n3. Therefore every gh equalsk(h₂h₁⁻¹h)∈kH, and conversely, so the two cosets are equal.\n\n4. Thus distinct cosets are disjoint and all cosets partitionG.", "role": "<p>Characterize when two cosets intersect.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Finite G and subgroup H; foundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>The left cosets give a disjoint partition of G.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: The left cosets give a disjoint partition of G.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Finite G and subgroup H; foundational imports stated in §1;\nkeep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Characterize when two cosets intersect.</p>", "Sense": "<p>No normality is needed for this set partition.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Every g belongs to gH since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gH\\cap kH</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=gh_{1}=kh_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k^{-1}g=h_{2}h_{1}^{-1}\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Therefore every gh equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k(h_{2}h_{1}^{-1}h)\\in kH</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand conversely, so the two cosets are equal.</p>", "<p>Thus distinct cosets are disjoint and all cosets partitionG.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>No normality is needed for this set partition. Publish only after\nchecking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: No normality is needed for this set\npartition. Recheck dependent nodes N2.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Equal coset sizes and counting", "proof": "1. For any g the mapH→gH, h↦gh, is surjective by definition and injective by left cancellation.\n\n2. Every coset has|H| elements.\n\n3. If there are[G:H] cosets, finite disjoint counting gives|G|=[G:H]|H|.\n\n4. Thus|H| divides|G|.\n\n5. The casesH={1} andH=G are included.", "role": "<p>Supply a bijection for each coset.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Partition and left multiplication; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Lagrange’s formula and divisibility.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: Lagrange’s formula and divisibility.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Partition and left multiplication; prior exports E1/v1; keep\ntheir assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Supply a bijection for each coset.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Divisibility is a necessary condition for subgroup order, not a\nuniversal existence theorem.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>For any g the map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H\\to gH</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\mapsto gh</annotation></semantics></math>,\nis surjective by definition and injective by left cancellation.</p>", "<p>Every coset has|H| elements.</p>", "<p>If there are[G:H] cosets, finite disjoint counting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gives|G|=[G:H]|H|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus|H| divides|G|.</p>", "<p>The cases\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=\\{1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=G</annotation></semantics></math>\nare included.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Divisibility is a necessary condition for subgroup order, not a\nuniversal existence theorem. Publish only after checking every displayed\ndeduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Divisibility is a necessary condition\nfor subgroup order, not a universal existence theorem. Withhold this\nterminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Equal coset sizes and counting", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Partition and left multiplication; prior\nexports E1/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-cosets-partition-the-group-1\">§4.N1 — Cosets partition the\ngroup</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Every g belongs to gH since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gH\\cap kH</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontains\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=gh_{1}=kh_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k^{-1}g=h_{2}h_{1}^{-1}\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Therefore every gh equals\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k(h_{2}h_{1}^{-1}h)\\in kH</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand conversely, so the two cosets are equal.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus distinct cosets are disjoint and all cosets\npartitionG.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-equal-coset-sizes-and-counting-1\">§4.N2 — Equal coset sizes\nand counting</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>For any g the map\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H\\to gH</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>↦</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h\\mapsto gh</annotation></semantics></math>,\nis surjective by definition and injective by left cancellation.</p></li>\n<li><p>Every coset has|H| elements.</p></li>\n<li><p>If there are[G:H] cosets, finite disjoint counting\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gives|G|=[G:H]|H|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus|H| divides|G|.</p></li>\n<li><p>The cases\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=\\{1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=G</annotation></semantics></math>\nare included.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>In\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>,\ntake\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H=\\{1,(12)\\}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nof order 2. Its left cosets are H,(13)H,(23)H, each with two elements,\ngiving\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">6=3\\cdot 2</annotation></semantics></math>.\nH is not normal, which confirms that normality is unnecessary for\nLagrange’s counting argument.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>A proposed quotient-group multiplication on these cosets requires\nnormality, which thisH lacks. Sense prevents a counting export from\nbeing used as a quotient-construction certificate; the partition remains\nvalid.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>A proposed quotient-group multiplication on these cosets requires\nnormality, which thisH lacks. Sense prevents a counting export from\nbeing used as a quotient-construction certificate; the partition remains\nvalid.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "45b5214da60e230b7aca6ad9cfc0a570bd2ea69d2246ba1b7f8b58692ed8bf86", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of lagrange’s theorem, with explicit\nmathematical contracts, local verification gates, and reusable\nexports.</p>", "references": "", "pdf": "reports/pdf/lagranges-theorem.pdf"}, {"id": "MA-02", "slug": "first-isomorphism-theorem-for-groups", "title": "First Isomorphism Theorem for Groups", "target": "<p>For a group homomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi:G\\to K</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ker\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>\nis normal and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G/\\ker\\varphi\\cong\\operatorname{im}\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Groups need not be finite. A homomorphism satisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (gh)=\\varphi (g)\\varphi (h)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor a normal subgroup N the quotient has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">multiplication(gN)(hN)=ghN</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe proof audits normality and representative independence before using\nthat construction.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Normal kernel and image subgroup", "proof": "1. The kernelN={g:φ(g)=1} contains1 and is closed under products and inverses.\n\n2. Forn∈N andg∈G, φ(gng⁻¹)=φ(g)1φ(g)⁻¹=1, soN is normal.\n\n3. The image contains1 and is closed under products and inverses, hence is a subgroup ofK.\n\n4. Quotient multiplication is valid becauseN is normal.", "role": "<p>Use inverse and conjugation identities.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi :G\\to K</annotation></semantics></math>\na homomorphism; foundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>A normal kernel N and subgroupim\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: A normal kernel N and subgroupim\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi :G\\to K</annotation></semantics></math>\na homomorphism; foundational imports stated in §1; keep their\nassumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use inverse and conjugation identities.</p>", "Sense": "<p>The theorem’s codomain conclusion is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im} \\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot all of K.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>The kernel\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=\\{g:\\varphi (g)=1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontains 1 and is closed under products and inverses.</p>", "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\in N</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\in G</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (gng</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi></mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^{-1})=\\varphi (g)1\\varphi (g)^{-1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso N is normal.</p>", "<p>The image contains 1 and is closed under products and inverses, hence\nis a subgroup of K.</p>", "<p>Quotient multiplication is valid because N is normal.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>The theorem’s codomain conclusion is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im} \\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot all of K. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: The theorem’s codomain conclusion is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{im} \\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>,\nnot all of K. Recheck dependent nodes N2, N3.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Induced map is well-defined", "proof": "1. If gN=hN thenh⁻¹g∈N, soφ(h)⁻¹φ(g)=1 and φ(g)=φ(h).\n\n2. ThusΦ is independent of representatives.\n\n3. It preserves multiplication sinceΦ(ghN)=φ(gh)=φ(g)φ(h)=Φ(gN)Φ(hN).\n\n4. It is ontoimφ by the definition of image.", "role": "<p>Check representative equality before algebra.</p>", "inputs": "<p>NormalN; proposed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi (gN)=\\varphi (g)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>A well-defined surjective homomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi :G/N\\to \\operatorname{im} \\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: A well-defined surjective homomorphism\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi :G/N\\to \\operatorname{im} \\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain NormalN; proposed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi (gN)=\\varphi (g)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Check representative equality before algebra.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A formula on cosets is not automatically well-defined.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gN=hN</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^{-1}g\\in N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (h)^{-1}\\varphi (g)=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (g)=\\varphi (h)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>\nis independent of representatives.</p>", "<p>It preserves multiplication since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi (ghN)=\\varphi (gh)=\\varphi (g)\\varphi (h)=\\Phi (gN)\\Phi (hN)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>It is ontoim\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>\nby the definition of image.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>A formula on cosets is not automatically well-defined. Publish only\nafter checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: A formula on cosets is not\nautomatically well-defined. Recheck dependent nodes N3.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Injectivity and isomorphism", "proof": "1. IfΦ(gN)=Φ(hN), thenφ(h⁻¹g)=1, so h⁻¹g∈N andgN=hN.\n\n2. HenceΦ is injective as well as surjective and a homomorphism.\n\n3. Its inverse preserves products because preimages are unique, so it is a group isomorphism.\n\n4. This proves G/kerφ≅imφ without any cardinality argument.", "role": "<p>Use equality of images to recover equality of cosets.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Induced\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1</p>", "export": "<p>The first isomorphism theorem for arbitrary groups.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: The first isomorphism theorem for arbitrary groups.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Induced\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use equality of images to recover equality of cosets.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Equal finite sizes cannot substitute for injectivity in infinite\ngroups.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi (gN)=\\Phi (hN)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (h^{-1}g)=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^{-1}g\\in N</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gN=hN</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>\nis injective as well as surjective and a homomorphism.</p>", "<p>Its inverse preserves products because preimages are unique, so it is\na group isomorphism.</p>", "<p>This proves\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G/\\operatorname{ker} \\varphi \\cong \\operatorname{im} \\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>\nwithout any cardinality argument.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>Equal finite sizes cannot substitute for injectivity in infinite\ngroups. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: Equal finite sizes cannot substitute\nfor injectivity in infinite groups. Withhold this terminal result until\nits gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Induced map is well-defined", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: NormalN; proposed\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi (gN)=\\varphi (g)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Injectivity and isomorphism", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Induced\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E2/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-normal-kernel-and-image-subgroup-1\">§4.N1 — Normal kernel and\nimage subgroup</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>The kernel\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N=\\{g:\\varphi (g)=1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>\ncontains 1 and is closed under products and inverses.</p></li>\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\in N</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g\\in G</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (gng</annotation></semantics></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi></mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^{-1})=\\varphi (g)1\\varphi (g)^{-1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso N is normal.</p></li>\n<li><p>The image contains 1 and is closed under products and inverses,\nhence is a subgroup of K.</p></li>\n<li><p>Quotient multiplication is valid because N is normal.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-induced-map-is-well-defined-1\">§4.N2 — Induced map is\nwell-defined</h3>\n<p>Define\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi:G/N\\to\\operatorname{im}\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>\nby\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi(gN)=\\varphi(g)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gN=hN</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^{-1}g\\in N</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (h)^{-1}\\varphi (g)=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (g)=\\varphi (h)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>\nis independent of representatives.</p></li>\n<li><p>It preserves multiplication since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi (ghN)=\\varphi (gh)=\\varphi (g)\\varphi (h)=\\Phi (gN)\\Phi (hN)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>It is ontoim\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>\nby the definition of image.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-injectivity-and-isomorphism-1\">§4.N3 — Injectivity and\nisomorphism</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi (gN)=\\Phi (hN)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (h^{-1}g)=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h^{-1}g\\in N</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gN=hN</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Phi</annotation></semantics></math>\nis injective as well as surjective and a homomorphism.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its inverse preserves products because preimages are unique, so\nit is a group isomorphism.</p></li>\n<li><p>This proves\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">im</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G/\\operatorname{ker} \\varphi \\cong \\operatorname{im} \\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>\nwithout any cardinality argument.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>Z</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>6</mn><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi :Z\\to Z/6Z</annotation></semantics></math>\nsending an integer to its residue,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ker</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{ker} \\varphi =6Z</annotation></semantics></math>\nandim\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>6</mn><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi =Z/6Z</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe induced map takes the additive cosetn+6Z to[n], giving the explicit\nisomorphism. For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi (n)=2n</annotation></semantics></math>\nintoZ, the image is 2Z, not the whole codomain.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>For the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>Z</mi><mo>↪</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">inclusion2Z\\hookrightarrow Z</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe kernel is 0; the quotient is 2Z and the theorem identifies it with\nits image 2Z. Sense rejects replacing the image by Z through the induced\ninclusion, since that map is not onto.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>For the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>Z</mi><mo>↪</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">inclusion2Z\\hookrightarrow Z</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe kernel is 0; the quotient is 2Z and the theorem identifies it with\nits image 2Z. Sense rejects replacing the image by Z through the induced\ninclusion, since that map is not onto.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "1373d1833e3bf18e131bd4bb45806a0b27c4c8fe4f07583fac5ed0aae19a5b40", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of first isomorphism theorem for\ngroups, with explicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates,\nand reusable exports.</p>", "references": "", "pdf": "reports/pdf/first-isomorphism-theorem-for-groups.pdf"}, {"id": "MA-03", "slug": "classification-groups-order-pq", "title": "Classification of Groups of Order pq", "target": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe primes. If p does not divide\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q-1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nevery group of order pq is isomorphic to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIf p divides\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q-1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthere are exactly two isomorphism classes:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand one nonabelian group\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>⋊</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_q\\rtimes C_p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<p>A complete classification must prove that every input group has one\nof the stated structures, construct each listed structure, and prove\nthat apparently different nontrivial constructions are isomorphic. Sylow\ncongruences alone do not close these obligations.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Sylow’s existence/counting theorems; Lagrange’s theorem; finite\nproduct-set counting; the theorem that the multiplicative group of the\nprime field\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nis cyclic of order\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q-1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe last result is the supporting primitive-root module, not an unstated\nassumption. Prime-order groups are cyclic because a nonidentity element\ngenerates a subgroup whose nontrivial order divides that prime.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Fix the classification domain", "proof": "Let $p<q$ be distinct primes and let $G$ have order $pq$. The classification must establish existence, exhaustion, and uniqueness of every isomorphism class, separately in the two divisibility regimes.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: The two possible regimes are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\nmid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|=pq</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nprime.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Primes, subgroup orders, Sylow counts</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Fix classification obligations</p>", "Sense": "<p>Require\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math></p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Fix the classification domain. Establish the following local result:\nThe two possible regimes are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\nmid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|=pq</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nprime.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Distinct primes, finite groups, and the stated classification\ntarget.</p>", "export": "<p>The two possible regimes are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\nmid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|G|=pq</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nprime.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Fix the ordered primes and the order of the group.</p>", "<p>Require existence and exhaustion, not just permitted Sylow\ncounts.</p>", "<p>Keep the cyclic class in both regimes.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Require\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Require\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nRecheck dependent nodes N2, N3, N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "A Unique Normal Subgroup of Order q", "proof": "Let n_q be the number of Sylow q-subgroups. Sylow gives $n_q\\mid p$ and $n_q\\equiv1\\pmod q$. Thus n_q is 1 or p. Since 1<p<q, p cannot be congruent to 1 modulo q. Hence n_q=1, and its unique subgroup Q is normal.\n\nChoose a Sylow p-subgroup P. Both Q and P are cyclic, of orders q and p respectively. Their intersection is trivial because its order divides both distinct primes. The product set QP has pq elements, hence equals G.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=QP</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q\\cong C_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nnormal,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\cong C_p</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q\\cap P=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Sylow q-count theorem</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Eliminate the larger candidate</p>", "Sense": "<p>Use count divides p</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>A Unique Normal Subgroup of Order q. Establish the following local\nresult:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=QP</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q\\cong C_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nnormal,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\cong C_p</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q\\cap P=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N1/E1; Sylow counting and subgroup product cardinalities.</p>", "export": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=QP</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q\\cong C_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nnormal,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P\\cong C_p</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q\\cap P=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Use\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_q\\mid p</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_q\\equiv1\\pmod q</annotation></semantics></math>\nto force\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_q=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Choose a Sylow\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>-subgroup\nand use coprime orders for trivial intersection.</p>", "<p>Count\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|QP|=pq</annotation></semantics></math>\nand conclude\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">QP=G</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Use count divides p Publish only after checking every displayed\ndeduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Use count divides p Recheck dependent\nnodes N3, N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Every Group Is Encoded by One Conjugation Action", "proof": "Choose generators x of Q and y of P. Every g in G has a unique expression $x^iy^j$, with i modulo q and j modulo p. Conjugation by y preserves Q, so\n\n$$yxy^{-1}=x^r$$\n\nfor nonzero r modulo q. Because y^p=1, repeated conjugation gives $r^p\\equiv1\\pmod q$.\n\nMultiplying normal forms gives\n\n$$(x^iy^j)(x^ky^l)=x^{i+r^jk}y^{j+l}.$$\n\nThus the group is completely determined by the action parameter r, and every group in the problem has such a parameter. Its order in F_q multiplicative is either 1 or p.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: Every group has normal forms\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^iy^j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yxy^{-1}=x^r</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^p\\equiv1\\pmod q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Prime-order cyclic groups</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Translate conjugation into exponent r</p>", "Sense": "<p>Check trivial intersection and full product</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Every Group Is Encoded by One Conjugation Action. Establish the\nfollowing local result: Every group has normal forms\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^iy^j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yxy^{-1}=x^r</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^p\\equiv1\\pmod q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N2/E2 and cyclicity of prime-order groups.</p>", "export": "<p>Every group has normal forms\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^iy^j</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yxy^{-1}=x^r</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^p\\equiv1\\pmod q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Choose generators of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Encode conjugation as a nonzero residue\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r</annotation></semantics></math>\nmodulo\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Derive\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(i,j)(k,l)=(i+r^jk,j+l)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the constraint\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^p=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>Check trivial intersection and full product Publish only after\nchecking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: Check trivial intersection and full\nproduct Recheck dependent nodes N4, N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N4", "title": "The Trivial Action Gives the Cyclic Class", "proof": "If r=1, x and y commute. The element xy has order pq: if (xy)^k=1, then x^k=y^(−k) lies in Q∩P, so both q and p divide k. Conversely (xy)^(pq)=1. Therefore G is cyclic of order pq.\n\nThis class exists for every pair of primes, including when p divides q−1.\n\n####  Construct and Verify the Nontrivial Class\n\nA nontrivial r with r^p=1 has order p. Such r exists exactly when p divides q−1, because F_q multiplicative is cyclic of that order.\n\nFor any such r, define a product on pairs $(i,j)\\in\\mathbb Z/q\\mathbb Z\\times\\mathbb Z/p\\mathbb Z$ by\n\n$$(i,j)(k,l)=(i+r^jk,j+l).$$\n\nThe condition r^p=1 makes the expression independent of the representative of j. Associativity holds because both ways of multiplying three pairs have first component $i+r^jk+r^{j+l}m$ and second component j+l+n. The identity is (0,0), and the inverse of (i,j) is $(−r^{-j}i,−j)$. Thus this is a group with pq elements.\n\nFor x=(1,0), y=(0,1), we have yx=(r,1) and xy=(1,1). Since r≠1, the group is nonabelian. This proves existence rather than merely permitting it.\n\n####  All Nontrivial Actions Give One Isomorphism Class\n\nA cyclic group has a unique subgroup of each order dividing its order. Therefore any two order-p elements r,r' of F_q multiplicative generate the same subgroup, and $r'=r^k$ for some k with 1≤k<p.\n\nIn the group constructed with parameter r, replace y by y^k. It still generates P because gcd(k,p)=1, and its action on x is exponent r^k=r'. Consequently the map from the r'-group sending (i,j) to $(i,kj)$ in the r-group respects the multiplication rule and is bijective. All nontrivial actions are therefore isomorphic.", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E4/v1: The trivial action gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>;\na nontrivial class exists exactly when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand all nontrivial actions yield one isomorphism class.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Cyclic Fq multiplicative group</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Classify homomorphisms\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Cp\\to \\operatorname{Aut} (Cq)</annotation></semantics></math></p>", "Sense": "<p>Separate permission, existence, and equivalence</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E4/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>The Trivial Action Gives the Cyclic Class. Establish the following\nlocal result: The trivial action gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>;\na nontrivial class exists exactly when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand all nontrivial actions yield one isomorphism class.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N3/E3 and cyclicity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb F_q^\\times</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "export": "<p>The trivial action gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>;\na nontrivial class exists exactly when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand all nontrivial actions yield one isomorphism class.</p>", "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove that commuting generators yield an element of order\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">pq</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>For an\norder-<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math>\nresidue, verify associativity, identity, inverses, and noncommutativity\nof the pair multiplication.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>′</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^{\\prime}=r^k</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\le k&lt;p</annotation></semantics></math>,\nuse\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>↦</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(i,j)\\mapsto(i,kj)</annotation></semantics></math>\nto identify the two constructed groups.</p>"], "exportId": "E4", "gate": "<p>Separate permission, existence, and equivalence Publish only after\nchecking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N4: Separate permission, existence, and\nequivalence Recheck dependent nodes N5.</p>"}, {"id": "N5", "title": "Exhaustion, Distinctness, and Branch Closure", "proof": "N3 shows every group is one of the action constructions. If p does not divide q−1, only r=1 is possible. If p divides q−1, the trivial and nontrivial constructions both exist, and N4C identifies all nontrivial ones. The two classes are distinct because one is abelian and the other is not. The classification follows. $\\square$", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E5/v1: There is one class if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\nmid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand exactly two if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>All action and decomposition evidence</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Join exhaustive branches</p>", "Sense": "<p>Keep cyclic case in both regimes</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E5/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "role": "<p>Exhaustion, Distinctness, and Branch Closure. Establish the following\nlocal result: There is one class if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\nmid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand exactly two if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "inputs": "<p>N3/E3 and N4/E4, including the construction and equivalence\ncertificates.</p>", "export": "<p>There is one class if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\nmid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand exactly two if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∣</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\mid(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "activities": ["<p>Every original group is encoded by one admissible action.</p>", "<p>The action classification supplies all possibilities and no duplicate\nnontrivial class.</p>", "<p>Distinguish the cyclic and nonabelian classes by commutativity.</p>"], "exportId": "E5", "gate": "<p>Keep cyclic case in both regimes Publish only after checking every\ndisplayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N5: Keep cyclic case in both regimes\nWithhold this terminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: A Unique Normal Subgroup of Order q", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N1/E1; Sylow counting and subgroup product\ncardinalities.</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Every Group Is Encoded by One Conjugation Action", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N2/E2 and cyclicity of prime-order\ngroups.</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N4", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N4: The Trivial Action Gives the Cyclic Class", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N3/E3 and cyclicity of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>×</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb F_q^\\times</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N5", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T4", "activity": "N5: Exhaustion, Distinctness, and Branch Closure", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N3/E3 and N4/E4, including the construction\nand equivalence certificates.</p>"}, {"source": "N4", "target": "N5", "export": "E4/v1", "id": "T5", "activity": "N5: Exhaustion, Distinctness, and Branch Closure", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: N3/E3 and N4/E4, including the construction\nand equivalence certificates.</p>"}], "proof": "<h3 id=\"n1-fix-the-classification-domain-1\">N1 — Fix the classification\ndomain</h3>\n<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe distinct primes and let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>\nhave order\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">pq</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe classification must establish existence, exhaustion, and uniqueness\nof every isomorphism class, separately in the two divisibility\nregimes.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n2-a-unique-normal-subgroup-of-order-q-1\">N2 — A Unique Normal\nSubgroup of Order q</h3>\n<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nbe the number of Sylow q-subgroups. Sylow gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_q\\mid p</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_q\\equiv1\\pmod q</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nis 1 or p. Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1&lt;p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>,\np cannot be congruent to 1 modulo q. Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_q=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand its unique subgroup Q is normal.</p>\n<p>Choose a Sylow p-subgroup P. Both Q and P are cyclic, of orders q and\np respectively. Their intersection is trivial because its order divides\nboth distinct primes. The product set QP has pq elements, hence equals\nG.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n3-every-group-is-encoded-by-one-conjugation-action-1\">N3 —\nEvery Group Is Encoded by One Conjugation Action</h3>\n<p>Choose generators x of Q and y of P. Every g in G has a unique\nexpression\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^iy^j</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwith i modulo q and j modulo p. Conjugation by y preserves Q, so</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yxy^{-1}=x^r</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>for nonzero r modulo q. Because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y^p=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nrepeated conjugation gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mod</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^p\\equiv1\\pmod q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<p>Multiplying normal forms gives</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x^iy^j)(x^ky^l)=x^{i+r^jk}y^{j+l}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>Thus the group is completely determined by the action parameter r,\nand every group in the problem has such a parameter. Its order in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nmultiplicative is either 1 or p.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n4-the-trivial-action-gives-the-cyclic-class-1\">N4 — The Trivial\nAction Gives the Cyclic Class</h3>\n<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nx and y commute. The element xy has order pq: if\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(xy)^k=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^k=y^{(-k)}</annotation></semantics></math>\nlies in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q\\cap P</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso both q and p divide k. Conversely\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(xy)^{(pq)}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nTherefore G is cyclic of order pq.</p>\n<p>This class exists for every pair of primes, including when p divides\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<h4 id=\"construct-and-verify-the-nontrivial-class-1\">Construct and\nVerify the Nontrivial Class</h4>\n<p>A nontrivial r with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^p=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas order p. Such r exists exactly when p divides\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q-1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nbecause\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nmultiplicative is cyclic of that order.</p>\n<p>For any such r, define a product on pairs\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(i,j)\\in\\mathbb Z/q\\mathbb Z\\times\\mathbb Z/p\\mathbb Z</annotation></semantics></math>\nby</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(i,j)(k,l)=(i+r^jk,j+l).</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>The condition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^p=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nmakes the expression independent of the representative of j.\nAssociativity holds because both ways of multiplying three pairs have\nfirst component\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i+r^jk+r^{j+l}m</annotation></semantics></math>\nand second component j+l+n. The identity is (0,0), and the inverse of\n(i,j) is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-r^{-j}i,-j)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus this is a group with pq elements.</p>\n<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=(1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,\nwe have\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yx=(r,1)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">xy=(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r\\ne 1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe group is nonabelian. This proves existence rather than merely\npermitting it.</p>\n<h4 id=\"all-nontrivial-actions-give-one-isomorphism-class-1\">All\nNontrivial Actions Give One Isomorphism Class</h4>\n<p>A cyclic group has a unique subgroup of each order dividing its\norder. Therefore any two order-p elements r,r’ of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F_q</annotation></semantics></math>\nmultiplicative generate the same subgroup, and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r&#39;=r^k</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor some k with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\le k&lt;p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<p>In the group constructed with parameter r, replace y by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y^k</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIt still generates P because\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">gcd</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{gcd} (k,p)=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand its action on x is exponent\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r^k=r</annotation></semantics></math>‘.\nConsequently the map from the r’-group sending (i,j) to\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(i,kj)</annotation></semantics></math>\nin the r-group respects the multiplication rule and is bijective. All\nnontrivial actions are therefore isomorphic.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n5-exhaustion-distinctness-and-branch-closure-1\">N5 —\nExhaustion, Distinctness, and Branch Closure</h3>\n<p>N3 shows every group is one of the action constructions. If p does\nnot divide\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q-1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nonly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=1</annotation></semantics></math>\nis possible. If p divides\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q-1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe trivial and nontrivial constructions both exist, and N4C identifies\nall nontrivial ones. The two classes are distinct because one is abelian\nand the other is not. The classification follows.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>▫</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>", "example": "<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 33%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 33%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Order</th>\n<th>Divisibility test</th>\n<th>Isomorphism classes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>3 does not divide 4</td>\n<td>C15 only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>2 divides 2</td>\n<td>C6 and the\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=-1</annotation></semantics></math>\nsemidirect product, isomorphic to S3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>21</td>\n<td>3 divides 6</td>\n<td>C21 and one nonabelian group</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>For order 21 choose\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=2</annotation></semantics></math>\nmodulo 7, since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{3}=8\\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\ne 1</annotation></semantics></math>.\nIts relation is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">yxy^{(-1)}=x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nChoosing\nr’<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">=4</annotation></semantics></math>\ninstead gives no new class: replace y by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nA concrete multiplication is</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1,1)(3,2)=(1+2\\cdot3,3)=(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>in residues modulo 7 and 3. These elements are inverses, consistent\nwith the general inverse formula.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>The assumption\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nidentifies which Sylow subgroup is forced normal. Equal primes lead to\norder\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a different classification. A nontrivial action does not eliminate\nthe trivial one. Distinct action parameters are not automatically\ndistinct isomorphism classes.</p>\n<p>Export normality of Q, the action normal form, semidirect\nconstruction, and the full classification. The resulting module\ndemonstrates structural branching, a concrete construction, and\nequivalence between apparently different solutions.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>A failed branch observes that Sylow allows\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n_p=q</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhen p divides\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q-1</annotation></semantics></math>\nand declares the classification finished.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Node:</strong> N5</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>State:</strong> STALLED</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Failing faculty:</strong> Action</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Missing obligations:</strong> [‘construct nonabelian\ngroup’, ‘prove all nontrivial actions equivalent’, ‘retain cyclic\nclass’]</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Repair target:</strong> N4</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Blocked export:</strong> exactly two isomorphism\nclasses</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Memory retrieves the automorphism-group structure. Sense\ndistinguishes an allowed count from an actual group. Intellect moves to\naction parameters. Action supplies the explicit pair group and\ngenerator-change isomorphism. Ego then combines exhaustion,\nconstruction, uniqueness, and distinctness. This closes the precise gap\nleft by the shorter classification sketch.</p>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>The assumption\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>\nidentifies which Sylow subgroup is forced normal. Equal primes lead to\norder\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand a different classification. A nontrivial action does not eliminate\nthe trivial one. Distinct action parameters are not automatically\ndistinct isomorphism classes.</p>\n<p>Export normality of Q, the action normal form, semidirect\nconstruction, and the full classification. The resulting module\ndemonstrates structural branching, a concrete construction, and\nequivalence between apparently different solutions.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": false, "sha256": "ace739f9e5255cc803a032b075959190251cf54cded9fa339abd5073926dbd02", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of classification of groups of order\npq, with explicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates, and\nreusable exports.</p>", "references": "<p><a\nhref=\"https://www-users.cse.umn.edu/~garrett/m/algebra/notes_2023-24/02.pdf\">University\nof Minnesota group theory notes: groups of order pq</a>.</p>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/classification-groups-order-pq.pdf"}, {"id": "MA-04", "slug": "fundamental-theorem-of-galois-theory", "title": "Fundamental Theorem of Galois Theory", "target": "<p>For a finite Galois extension\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L/K</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith group\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nprove an inclusion-reversing bijection between intermediate fields\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math>\nand subgroups\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H\\le G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nvia\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>↦</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Gal</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\mapsto\\operatorname{Gal}(L/E)</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>↦</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H\\mapsto L^H</annotation></semantics></math>.\nProve\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[L:L^H]=|H|</annotation></semantics></math>\nand normal subgroups correspond to intermediate extensions Galois over\nK, with quotient group\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G/H</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "imports": ["<p>L/K is a finite normal separable extension,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=\\operatorname{Aut} _K(L)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nImport: (i) finite Galois extensions have automorphism count equal to\ndegree; (ii) Artin’s fixed-field theorem, for a finite automorphism\nsubgroup H,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[L:L^H]=|H|</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L/L^H</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Galois; (iii) the tower law; (iv) embeddings of an intermediate field\ninto an algebraic closure extend to L, and K-normality sendsL to itself.\nThese are substantive field-theory imports, not the correspondence being\nproved.</p>\n<p>The last step also imports the first isomorphism theorem (MA-02).</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Field-to-group recovery", "proof": "1. L/E remains normal and separable: L is a splitting field overK of separable polynomials and hence also a splitting field of those polynomials overE.\n\n2. Set H_E=Aut_E(L); the automorphism-count import gives|H_E|=[L:E].\n\n3. Certainly E⊂L^{H_E}.\n\n4. Artin gives[L:L^{H_E}]=|H_E|=[L:E].\n\n5. The tower law then forces[L^{H_E}:E]=1, soL^{H_E}=E.", "role": "<p>Compare degrees after forming its fixing subgroup.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Intermediate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K\\subset E\\subset L</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>The field recovered from its fixing subgroup is exactlyE.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: The field recovered from its fixing subgroup is\nexactlyE.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Intermediate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K\\subset E\\subset L</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Compare degrees after forming its fixing subgroup.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Inclusion alone is not enough; degree equality closes recovery.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>L/E remains normal and separable: L is a splitting field over K of\nseparable polynomials and hence also a splitting field of those\npolynomials over E.</p>", "<p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_E=\\operatorname{Aut} _E(L)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe automorphism-count import\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gives|H_E|=[L:E]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Certainly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\subset L^{H_E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Artin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gives[L:L^{H_E}]=|H_E|=[L:E]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The tower law then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msup><mo>:</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">forces[L^{H_E}:E]=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L^{H_E}=E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>Inclusion alone is not enough; degree equality closes recovery.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: Inclusion alone is not enough; degree\nequality closes recovery. Recheck dependent nodes N2, N3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Group-to-field recovery", "proof": "1. H fixesE_H pointwise, so H⊂Aut_{E_H}(L).\n\n2. Artin saysL/E_H is Galois and its degree is|H|.\n\n3. Thus its full automorphism group has|H| elements and equalsH.\n\n4. The two constructions are therefore mutual inverses.\n\n5. If E₁⊂E₂ then every automorphism fixingE₂ fixesE₁, soH_{E₂}⊂H_{E₁}; ifH₁⊂H₂ thenL^{H₂}⊂L^{H₁}.\n\n6. This proves the inclusion-reversing bijection.", "role": "<p>Compare the group sizes supplied by Artin.</p>", "inputs": "<p>SubgroupH\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\le G</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_H=L^H</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>Both inverse identities and the degree\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">formula[L:L^H]=|H|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: Both inverse identities and the degree\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">formula[L:L^H]=|H|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain SubgroupH\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\le G</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_H=L^H</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Compare the group sizes supplied by Artin.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Fixing all of E is stronger than preservingE as a set.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>H fixes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_H</annotation></semantics></math>\npointwise, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H\\subset \\operatorname{Aut} _{E_H}(L)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Artin says\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L/E_H</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Galois and its degree is|H|.</p>", "<p>Thus its full automorphism group has|H| elements and equals H.</p>", "<p>The two constructions are therefore mutual inverses.</p>", "<p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{1}\\subset E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen every automorphism fixing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nfixes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_{E_{2}}\\subset H_{E_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nif\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_{1}\\subset H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L^{H_{2}}\\subset L^{H_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>This proves the inclusion-reversing bijection.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>Fixing all of E is stronger than preservingE as a set. Publish only\nafter checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: Fixing all of E is stronger than\npreservingE as a set. Recheck dependent nodes N3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Normal subgroups and normal fields", "proof": "1. Forσ∈G, the fixing subgroup of σ(E) is σH_Eσ⁻¹, so the correspondence makesH_E normal exactly whenσ(E)=E for everyσ.\n\n2. If E/K is normal, each suchσ preservesE.\n\n3. Conversely everyK-embedding ofE extends to aK-embedding ofL and thus to an element ofG; stability then makes all conjugates ofE equalE, proving normality.\n\n4. Separability descends fromL/K, so this is precisely the Galois condition onE/K.", "role": "<p>Translate conjugation to stability of the fixed field.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Correspondence and extension of embeddings; prior exports E1/v1,\nE2/v1</p>", "export": "<p>H normal in G iff its fixed field is Galois over K.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: H normal in G iff its fixed field is Galois over K.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Correspondence and extension of embeddings; prior exports\nE1/v1, E2/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Translate conjugation to stability of the fixed field.</p>", "Sense": "<p>All embeddings, not just a few automorphisms, must be controlled.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma \\in G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe fixing subgroup of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma (E)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma H_E\\sigma ^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the correspondence makes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_E</annotation></semantics></math>\nnormal exactly when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma (E)=E</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>If E/K is normal, each such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\npreserves E.</p>", "<p>Conversely every K-embedding of E extends to aK-embedding of L and\nthus to an element of G; stability then makes all conjugates of E equal\nE, proving normality.</p>", "<p>Separability descends from L/K, so this is precisely the Galois\ncondition on E/K.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>All embeddings, not just a few automorphisms, must be controlled.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: All embeddings, not just a few\nautomorphisms, must be controlled. Recheck dependent nodes N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N4", "title": "Restriction quotient", "proof": "1. Restriction res:G→Aut_K(E) is defined becauseE is stable.\n\n2. Its kernel consists exactly of automorphisms fixingE, namelyH.\n\n3. AnyK-automorphism ofE extends toL; normality ofL/K makes the extension an element ofG, so res is onto.\n\n4. By MA-02, G/H≅Aut_K(E)=Gal(E/K).\n\n5. This closes the entire theorem.", "role": "<p>Check surjectivity using embedding extension.</p>", "inputs": "<p>NormalH and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=L^H</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E3/v1</p>", "export": "<p>The normal-field quotient identification\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Gal</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G/H\\cong \\operatorname{Gal} (E/K)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E4/v1: The normal-field quotient identification\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Gal</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G/H\\cong \\operatorname{Gal} (E/K)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain NormalH and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=L^H</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E3/v1; keep their assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Check surjectivity using embedding extension.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Without normality restriction need not land in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Aut} _K(E)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E4/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Restriction\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{res} :G\\to \\operatorname{Aut} _K(E)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis defined because E is stable.</p>", "<p>Its kernel consists exactly of automorphisms fixing E, namelyH.</p>", "<p>AnyK-automorphism of E extends to L; normality of L/K makes the\nextension an element of G, so res is onto.</p>", "<p>By MA-02,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Gal</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G/H\\cong \\operatorname{Aut} _K(E)=\\operatorname{Gal} (E/K)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>This closes the entire theorem.</p>"], "exportId": "E4", "gate": "<p>Without normality restriction need not land in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Aut} _K(E)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nPublish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N4: Without normality restriction need not\nland in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Aut} _K(E)</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWithhold this terminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Group-to-field recovery", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: SubgroupH\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\le G</annotation></semantics></math>;\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_H=L^H</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E1/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N1", "target": "N3", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Normal subgroups and normal fields", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Correspondence and extension of embeddings;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N3: Normal subgroups and normal fields", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Correspondence and extension of embeddings;\nprior exports E1/v1, E2/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N4", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T4", "activity": "N4: Restriction quotient", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: NormalH and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E=L^H</annotation></semantics></math>;\nprior exports E3/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-field-to-group-recovery-1\">§4.N1 — Field-to-group\nrecovery</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>L/E remains normal and separable: L is a splitting field over K\nof separable polynomials and hence also a splitting field of those\npolynomials over E.</p></li>\n<li><p>Set\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_E=\\operatorname{Aut} _E(L)</annotation></semantics></math>;\nthe automorphism-count import\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gives|H_E|=[L:E]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Certainly\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E\\subset L^{H_E}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Artin\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">gives[L:L^{H_E}]=|H_E|=[L:E]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The tower law then\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msup><mo>:</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">forces[L^{H_E}:E]=1</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L^{H_E}=E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-group-to-field-recovery-1\">§4.N2 — Group-to-field\nrecovery</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>H fixes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_H</annotation></semantics></math>\npointwise, so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H\\subset \\operatorname{Aut} _{E_H}(L)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Artin says\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L/E_H</annotation></semantics></math>\nis Galois and its degree is|H|.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus its full automorphism group has|H| elements and equals\nH.</p></li>\n<li><p>The two constructions are therefore mutual inverses.</p></li>\n<li><p>If\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{1}\\subset E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen every automorphism fixing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nfixes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_{E_{2}}\\subset H_{E_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nif\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_{1}\\subset H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nthen\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L^{H_{2}}\\subset L^{H_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>This proves the inclusion-reversing bijection.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-normal-subgroups-and-normal-fields-1\">§4.N3 — Normal\nsubgroups and normal fields</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma \\in G</annotation></semantics></math>,\nthe fixing subgroup of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma (E)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma H_E\\sigma ^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso the correspondence makes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_E</annotation></semantics></math>\nnormal exactly when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma (E)=E</annotation></semantics></math>\nfor every\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>If E/K is normal, each such\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\npreserves E.</p></li>\n<li><p>Conversely every K-embedding of E extends to aK-embedding of L\nand thus to an element of G; stability then makes all conjugates of E\nequal E, proving normality.</p></li>\n<li><p>Separability descends from L/K, so this is precisely the Galois\ncondition on E/K.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n4-restriction-quotient-1\">§4.N4 — Restriction quotient</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Restriction\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">res</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo>:</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{res} :G\\to \\operatorname{Aut} _K(E)</annotation></semantics></math>\nis defined because E is stable.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its kernel consists exactly of automorphisms fixing E,\nnamelyH.</p></li>\n<li><p>AnyK-automorphism of E extends to L; normality of L/K makes the\nextension an element of G, so res is onto.</p></li>\n<li><p>By MA-02,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>≅</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Aut</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Gal</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G/H\\cong \\operatorname{Aut} _K(E)=\\operatorname{Gal} (E/K)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>This closes the entire theorem.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>Let\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=Q(\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{3)}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K=Q</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe four sign changes form\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C_{2}\\times C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe subgroup fixing\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nconsists of the identity and the change\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>↦</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt{3\\mapsto }-\\sqrt{3}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nits fixed field is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q(\\sqrt{2)}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">and[L:Q(\\sqrt{2)]}=2=|H|</annotation></semantics></math>.\nAll subgroups are normal and the restriction quotient has order 2.</p>", "boundary": ["<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mroot><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q(\\sqrt[3]{}2)/Q</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not normal: its nonreal conjugate roots are absent and\nitsQ-automorphism group is trivial. Its fixed field under that trivial\ngroup is the whole extension, notQ. Sense blocks using this extension in\nthe finite Galois correspondence.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mroot><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>/</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Q(\\sqrt[3]{}2)/Q</annotation></semantics></math>\nis not normal: its nonreal conjugate roots are absent and\nitsQ-automorphism group is trivial. Its fixed field under that trivial\ngroup is the whole extension, notQ. Sense blocks using this extension in\nthe finite Galois correspondence.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "9be8e5c26add2b942b2a36598fd6cd70423bd677bf13bc7c6748bd08afa100e9", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of fundamental theorem of galois\ntheory, with explicit mathematical contracts, local verification gates,\nand reusable exports.</p>", "references": "<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/res-18-012-algebra-ii-student-notes-spring-2022/pages/student-notes/\">MIT\nAlgebra II notes: field extensions and Galois theory</a>.</li>\n</ul>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/fundamental-theorem-of-galois-theory.pdf"}, {"id": "MA-05", "slug": "abelruffini-theorem-via-an-explicit-quintic", "title": "Abel–Ruffini Theorem via an Explicit Quintic", "target": "<p>Prove\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(x)=x^5-4x+2\\in\\mathbb Q[x]</annotation></semantics></math>\nhas Galois group\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_5</annotation></semantics></math>\nand is not solvable by radicals. Deduce there is no radical formula\nsolving every quintic.</p>", "imports": ["<p>Use Eisenstein’s criterion: a primitive integer polynomial with all\nnonleading coefficients divisible by a prime\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,\nleading coefficient not divisible by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>ℓ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand constant coefficient not divisible by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell ^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible over Q. Import characteristic-zero splitting-field Galois\ntheory, transitivity for irreducible polynomials, orbit–stabilizer,\nCauchy’s group theorem, Lagrange’s theorem, and the radical-solvability\ncriterion: a polynomial over Q is solvable by radicals iff its\nsplitting-field Galois group is solvable. The permutation generation and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nnonsolvability steps are established below.</p>"], "nodes": [{"id": "N1", "title": "Irreducibility and real-root count", "proof": "1. Eisenstein at 2 applies: the coefficients0,0,0,−4,2 are divisible by 2 and the constant2 is not divisible by 4.\n\n2. Thusf is irreducible.\n\n3. Its derivative5x⁴−4 vanishes at±α whereα=(4/5)^{1/4}; it is positive outside and negative inside.\n\n4. Since α>5/8, f(α)=2−(16/5)α<0 andf(−α)=2+(16/5)α>0.\n\n5. The limits at−∞ and∞ are−∞ and∞.\n\n6. Strict monotonicity on the three intervals therefore gives exactly three distinct real roots and two nonreal roots forming one conjugate pair.\n\n7. Irreducibility over Q in characteristic zero supplies separability, so all five complex roots are distinct.", "role": "<p>Combine Eisenstein with exact critical-point signs.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=x^{5}-4x+2</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1</p>", "export": "<p>An irreducible quintic with three real roots and one conjugate\npair.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E1/v1: An irreducible quintic with three real roots and one\nconjugate pair.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f=x^{5}-4x+2</annotation></semantics></math>;\nfoundational imports stated in §1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Combine Eisenstein with exact critical-point signs.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A plotted root count alone is not an exact certificate.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E1/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Eisenstein at 2 applies: the coefficients\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0,0,0,-4,2</annotation></semantics></math>\nare divisible by 2 and the constant 2 is not divisible by 4.</p>", "<p>Thusf is irreducible.</p>", "<p>Its derivative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5x^{4}-4</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>±</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pm \\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha =(4/5)^{1/4}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nit is positive outside and negative inside.</p>", "<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha &gt;5/8</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(\\alpha )=2-(16/5)\\alpha &lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(-\\alpha )=2+(16/5)\\alpha &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>The limits at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>∞</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nare\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>∞</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Strict monotonicity on the three intervals therefore gives exactly\nthree distinct real roots and two nonreal roots forming one conjugate\npair.</p>", "<p>Irreducibility over Q in characteristic zero supplies separability,\nso all five complex roots are distinct.</p>"], "exportId": "E1", "gate": "<p>A plotted root count alone is not an exact certificate. Publish only\nafter checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N1: A plotted root count alone is not an\nexact certificate. Recheck dependent nodes N2, N3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N2", "title": "Two permutation types", "proof": "1. Let G be the splitting-field Galois group acting faithfully on five roots.\n\n2. Irreducibility gives a transitive action, so5 divides|G| by orbit–stabilizer.\n\n3. Cauchy supplies an element of order5, necessarily a5-cycle inS₅.\n\n4. Complex conjugation is an automorphism of the splitting field fixingQ; it fixes the three real roots and swaps the nonreal pair, hence is a transposition.", "role": "<p>Read transitivity and complex conjugation.</p>", "inputs": "<p>Irreducibility and real-root count; prior exports E1/v1</p>", "export": "<p>G contains a5-cycle and a transposition.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E2/v1: G contains a5-cycle and a transposition.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain Irreducibility and real-root count; prior exports E1/v1; keep\ntheir assumptions and versions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Read transitivity and complex conjugation.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A nonreal-root pair count determines the entire conjugation\npermutation.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E2/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Let G be the splitting-field Galois group acting faithfully on five\nroots.</p>", "<p>Irreducibility gives a transitive action, so 5 divides|G| by\norbit–stabilizer.</p>", "<p>Cauchy supplies an element of order 5, necessarily a5-cycle in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>Complex conjugation is an automorphism of the splitting field fixing\nQ; it fixes the three real roots and swaps the nonreal pair, hence is a\ntransposition.</p>"], "exportId": "E2", "gate": "<p>A nonreal-root pair count determines the entire conjugation\npermutation. Publish only after checking every displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N2: A nonreal-root pair count determines\nthe entire conjugation permutation. Recheck dependent nodes N3, N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N3", "title": "Generate the full symmetric group", "proof": "1. Label the roots cyclically soσ acts by addition1 modulo5, and writeτ=(a,b) with nonzero differenceb−a mod5.\n\n2. Its conjugatesσ^jτσ^(−j) swap the translated pairs(a+j,b+j).\n\n3. These edges form a connected graph since repeated addition of a nonzero residue visits all five vertices.\n\n4. Edge transpositions on a connected graph generate every transposition: along a path, conjugating the final edge swap by the preceding path swaps gives a swap between the endpoints.\n\n5. All transpositions generateS₅, soS₅⊂G⊂S₅ andG=S₅.", "role": "<p>Use conjugate transpositions as edges in a connected graph.</p>", "inputs": "<p>A5-cycle\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nand transposition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau</annotation></semantics></math>\nin G; prior exports E2/v1</p>", "export": "<p>The exact Galois group is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E3/v1: The exact Galois group is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain A5-cycle\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nand transposition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau</annotation></semantics></math>\nin G; prior exports E2/v1; keep their assumptions and versions\nattached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Use conjugate transpositions as edges in a connected graph.</p>", "Sense": "<p>A cycle/transposition claim needs the connected-graph proof; it is\nnot automatic for arbitrary cycle lengths.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E3/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>Label the roots cyclically so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nacts by addition1 modulo 5, and write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau =(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith nonzero differenceb\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-a</annotation></semantics></math>\nmod 5.</p>", "<p>Its conjugates\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>τ</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma ^j\\tau \\sigma ^{(-j)}</annotation></semantics></math>\nswap the translated pair\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s(a+j,b+j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>These edges form a connected graph since repeated addition of a\nnonzero residue visits all five vertices.</p>", "<p>Edge transpositions on a connected graph generate every\ntransposition: along a path, conjugating the final edge swap by the\npreceding path swaps gives a swap between the endpoints.</p>", "<p>All transpositions generateS\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi></mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}\\subset G\\subset S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"], "exportId": "E3", "gate": "<p>A cycle/transposition claim needs the connected-graph proof; it is\nnot automatic for arbitrary cycle lengths. Publish only after checking\nevery displayed deduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N3: A cycle/transposition claim needs the\nconnected-graph proof; it is not automatic for arbitrary cycle lengths.\nRecheck dependent nodes N4.</p>"}, {"id": "N4", "title": "Nonsolvability and radical obstruction", "proof": "1. InA₅ the conjugacy-class sizes are1,15 (double transpositions),20 (3-cycles), and 12,12 (the two classes of 5-cycles).\n\n2. They follow from cycle counting and centralizer sizes4,3,5 inA₅.\n\n3. A normal subgroup is a union of these classes containing the identity, and its order divides60.\n\n4. The possible such sums are1,13,25,16,28,40,21,33,45,36,48,60; only1 and 60 divide60.\n\n5. Thus A₅ is simple.\n\n6. It is nonabelian, so its nontrivial commutator subgroup, being normal, is allA₅; its derived series never reaches1.\n\n7. Hence A₅, and thereforeS₅ which contains it, is not solvable.\n\n8. By the imported radical criterion the quintic is not solvable by radicals.\n\n9. A radical formula for every quintic would solve this one, contradiction.", "role": "<p>Prove the needed group obstruction before applying the field\ntheorem.</p>", "inputs": "<p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nradical criterion; prior exports E3/v1</p>", "export": "<p>This explicit quintic is not solvable by radicals; no radical formula\ncovers every quintic.</p>", "faculties": {"Ego": "<p>Own E4/v1: This explicit quintic is not solvable by radicals; no\nradical formula covers every quintic.</p>", "Memory": "<p>Retain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nradical criterion; prior exports E3/v1; keep their assumptions and\nversions attached.</p>", "Intellect": "<p>Prove the needed group obstruction before applying the field\ntheorem.</p>", "Sense": "<p>Some quintics are solvable; the conclusion is not a claim about every\nindividual quintic.</p>", "Action": "<p>Carry out the numbered deductions and publish E4/v1 together with its\nhypotheses and proof location.</p>"}, "activities": ["<p>In\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe conjugacy-class sizes are 1,15 (double transpositions),20\n(3-cycles), and 12,12 (the two classes of 5-cycles).</p>", "<p>They follow from cycle counting and centralizer sizes4,3,5 in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>", "<p>A normal subgroup is a union of these classes containing the\nidentity, and its order divides60.</p>", "<p>The possible such sums are 1,13,25,16,28,40,21,33,45,36,48,60; only1\nand 60 divide60.</p>", "<p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis simple.</p>", "<p>It is nonabelian, so its nontrivial commutator subgroup, being\nnormal, is all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nits derived series never reaches1.</p>", "<p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhich contains it, is not solvable.</p>", "<p>By the imported radical criterion the quintic is not solvable by\nradicals.</p>", "<p>A radical formula for every quintic would solve this one,\ncontradiction.</p>"], "exportId": "E4", "gate": "<p>Some quintics are solvable; the conclusion is not a claim about every\nindividual quintic. Publish only after checking every displayed\ndeduction.</p>", "repair": "<p>If the check fails, revise N4: Some quintics are solvable; the\nconclusion is not a claim about every individual quintic. Withhold this\nterminal result until its gate passes.</p>"}], "edges": [{"source": "N1", "target": "N2", "export": "E1/v1", "id": "T1", "activity": "N2: Two permutation types", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: Irreducibility and real-root count; prior\nexports E1/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N2", "target": "N3", "export": "E2/v1", "id": "T2", "activity": "N3: Generate the full symmetric group", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract: A5-cycle\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nand transposition\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau</annotation></semantics></math>\nin G; prior exports E2/v1</p>"}, {"source": "N3", "target": "N4", "export": "E3/v1", "id": "T3", "activity": "N4: Nonsolvability and radical obstruction", "gate": "<p>Use the same mathematical objects and hypotheses as the source\nexport. Receiving contract:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nradical criterion; prior exports E3/v1</p>"}], "proof": "<p>Read these steps in order as one proof; the diagram is optional.\nNumbered activities identify the specific constructions and deductions\nowned by each node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"n1-irreducibility-and-real-root-count-1\">§4.N1 — Irreducibility\nand real-root count</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Eisenstein at 2 applies: the coefficients\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>−</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0,0,0,-4,2</annotation></semantics></math>\nare divisible by 2 and the constant 2 is not divisible by 4.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thusf is irreducible.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its derivative\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">5x^{4}-4</annotation></semantics></math>\nvanishes at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>±</mi><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pm \\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhere\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha =(4/5)^{1/4}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nit is positive outside and negative inside.</p></li>\n<li><p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha &gt;5/8</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(\\alpha )=2-(16/5)\\alpha &lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(-\\alpha )=2+(16/5)\\alpha &gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>The limits at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>∞</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nare\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>∞</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Strict monotonicity on the three intervals therefore gives\nexactly three distinct real roots and two nonreal roots forming one\nconjugate pair.</p></li>\n<li><p>Irreducibility over Q in characteristic zero supplies\nseparability, so all five complex roots are distinct.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n2-two-permutation-types-1\">§4.N2 — Two permutation types</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Let G be the splitting-field Galois group acting faithfully on\nfive roots.</p></li>\n<li><p>Irreducibility gives a transitive action, so 5 divides|G| by\norbit–stabilizer.</p></li>\n<li><p>Cauchy supplies an element of order 5, necessarily a5-cycle in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>Complex conjugation is an automorphism of the splitting field\nfixing Q; it fixes the three real roots and swaps the nonreal pair,\nhence is a transposition.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n3-generate-the-full-symmetric-group-1\">§4.N3 — Generate the\nfull symmetric group</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>Label the roots cyclically so\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>\nacts by addition1 modulo 5, and write\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau =(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>\nwith nonzero differenceb\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-a</annotation></semantics></math>\nmod 5.</p></li>\n<li><p>Its conjugates\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>τ</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>−</mi><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma ^j\\tau \\sigma ^{(-j)}</annotation></semantics></math>\nswap the translated pair\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s(a+j,b+j)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>These edges form a connected graph since repeated addition of a\nnonzero residue visits all five vertices.</p></li>\n<li><p>Edge transpositions on a connected graph generate every\ntransposition: along a path, conjugating the final edge swap by the\npreceding path swaps gives a swap between the endpoints.</p></li>\n<li><p>All transpositions generateS\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi></mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nso\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}\\subset G\\subset S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G=S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"n4-nonsolvability-and-radical-obstruction-1\">§4.N4 —\nNonsolvability and radical obstruction</h3>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p>In\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nthe conjugacy-class sizes are 1,15 (double transpositions),20\n(3-cycles), and 12,12 (the two classes of 5-cycles).</p></li>\n<li><p>They follow from cycle counting and centralizer sizes4,3,5 in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p>A normal subgroup is a union of these classes containing the\nidentity, and its order divides60.</p></li>\n<li><p>The possible such sums are 1,13,25,16,28,40,21,33,45,36,48,60;\nonly1 and 60 divide60.</p></li>\n<li><p>Thus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nis simple.</p></li>\n<li><p>It is nonabelian, so its nontrivial commutator subgroup, being\nnormal, is all\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>;\nits derived series never reaches1.</p></li>\n<li><p>Hence\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>,\nand therefore\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>\nwhich contains it, is not solvable.</p></li>\n<li><p>By the imported radical criterion the quintic is not solvable by\nradicals.</p></li>\n<li><p>A radical formula for every quintic would solve this one,\ncontradiction.</p></li>\n</ol>", "example": "<p>The critical-point audit uses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.9457</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha \\approx 0.9457</annotation></semantics></math>\nonly as an illustration; the exact inequality\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha &gt;5/8</annotation></semantics></math>\nproves the signs. By contrastx\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi></mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^{5}-2</annotation></semantics></math>\nis irreducible but has roots expressed by a fifth root and roots of\nunity, so irreducibility alone cannot imply nonsolvability.</p>", "boundary": ["<p>A candidate exports “irreducible quintic\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>⇒</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Longrightarrow G=S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.”\nSense counters with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^{5}-2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand with smaller transitive groups. The repaired route retains both the\n5-cycle and single transposition, proves connected generation, and only\nthen invokes the radical obstruction.</p>"], "repair": [{"label": "Failure and correction", "html": "<p>This is an authored teaching trace, not a recorded agent run.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Ego\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nMemory:</strong> register the §1 theorem, imports, and requested exports\nbefore beginning the proof.</li>\n<li><strong>Intellect\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nAction:</strong> choose the bridges in §3 and carry out the numbered\nactivities in §4; transmit only established E-exports along the §2\nDAG.</li>\n<li><strong>Sense\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math>\nresponsible node:</strong> test the specific boundary/failure in §5 and\nthe node’s individual audit. A failing candidate is withheld; downstream\nnodes may not use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory + Intellect:</strong> identify whether the error is\nan omitted condition, an invalid inference, or an attempted extension\nbeyond the theorem. Restore the exact contract or explicitly state a\ndifferent one.</li>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> redo the affected mathematical activity\nusing the repaired condition or inference. Recheck consuming nodes,\nrather than feeding their conclusions back as premises.</li>\n<li><strong>Ego:</strong> publish only the supported export with its\nassumptions and proof location. A hypothetical revised export is v2; the\nwritten proof here is the v1 exposition, not a claim that this repair\nwas executed.</li>\n</ol>"}, {"label": "Hypothesis boundary", "html": "<p>A candidate exports “irreducible quintic\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>⇒</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Longrightarrow G=S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.”\nSense counters with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x^{5}-2</annotation></semantics></math>\nand with smaller transitive groups. The repaired route retains both the\n5-cycle and single transposition, proves connected generation, and only\nthen invokes the radical obstruction.</p>"}, {"label": "Version and recheck", "html": "<p>Treat any changed assumption as a new contract. Recheck the revised\nexport and all of its descendants. A backward diagnostic never\nestablishes an earlier theorem. This is an authored teaching trace, not\nan execution log.</p>"}], "standard": true, "sha256": "151f247868d39b24c9d6419a55283c30feeb8e4970df4012c3b2f32fdae3ebd8", "idea": "<p>A complete authored walkthrough of abel–ruffini theorem via an\nexplicit quintic, with explicit mathematical contracts, local\nverification gates, and reusable exports.</p>", "references": "<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/res-18-012-algebra-ii-student-notes-spring-2022/pages/student-notes/\">MIT\nAlgebra II notes: field extensions and Galois theory</a>.</li>\n</ul>", "pdf": "reports/pdf/abelruffini-theorem-via-an-explicit-quintic.pdf"}], "links": [{"source": "MA-01", "target": "MA-03", "label": "Subgroup orders", "detail": "Lagrange and coprime orders force the Sylow intersection to be trivial."}, {"source": "MA-02", "target": "MA-04", "label": "Quotient isomorphism", "detail": "The restriction homomorphism yields G/H ≅ Gal(E/K)."}, {"source": "MA-01", "target": "MA-05", "label": "Order divisibility", "detail": "Normal-subgroup orders in A₅ must divide 60."}], "evidence": "Authored proof walkthroughs. No deployed agent execution or formal kernel verification is claimed."};
